# CLAUDE.md

Per-repo orientation for `${project_org}/${project_name}` — non-IaC,
non-k8s homelab configuration (Talos, network, Proxmox, servers).

## Homelab universals

- **Toolchain pinned via `mise.toml`**; task runner `just`.
- **`.env` is a [1Password Developer Environment](https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/local-env-file)** file. `op run --env-file=.env -- <cmd>`. Never `source .env`.
- **`docz create <type> "Title"`** for new docs.
- **Capture cross-cutting surprises in the active IMPL's Follow-Ups**.
- **`grep` is `rg`** — drop `-E`.

## Repo layout

```
talos/                # Talos node configs, version pins, extension manifests
network/              # network topology, switch configs, VLAN/subnet docs
proxmox/              # Proxmox host config, storage notes, cluster layout
servers/              # bare-metal server inventory + provisioning notes
```

## Conventions

- **This is the catch-all for "config that isn't k8s manifests or
  Terraform"**. If it could live in `${project_org}/tf-live` (i.e. it
  belongs in `infra-live/`), put it there instead. This repo is for
  source-of-truth notes, manifests, and bootstrap material consumed by
  *humans* or by tf-live regeneration recipes.
- **Talos extensions / version pins** drive
  `${project_org}/tf-live`'s Talos VM templating. Pin Talos version
  + extension SHAs here; tf-live's boilerplate templates read from this
  repo's `talos/versions.yaml` (or equivalent).
- **Network topology** is documented (not generated). `network/` holds
  Mermaid diagrams + switch config exports + VLAN/subnet allocations.
  Cross-link from `${project_org}/docs` for visibility.
- **Server inventory** in `servers/` mirrors physical reality: model,
  serial, role, last-touched. Updated when hardware changes —
  Ansible-style automation lives in `tf-live` if/when it shows up.

## Workflow

- **For Talos node config changes**: edit `talos/` here, then
  regenerate `infra-live/talos/*` via
  `cd ../tf-live && just talos <role>`. The boilerplate templates pull
  pinned versions/extensions from this repo via file:// reference.
- **For network changes**: document first (PR to this repo), then apply
  via Technitium / Unifi UI (or terraform-provider-unifi from tf-live).
- **For new physical hardware**: add to `servers/inventory.md`, then
  decide whether it joins Proxmox (`proxmox/`), Talos
  (`talos/cluster-membership.md`), or stays standalone.

